      "source": "https://youmeky.ai/towns/hazel"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Hazel is the birthplace of 1960s singer-songwriter Jackie DeShannon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazel%2C_Kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town of Hazel was founded as a stop on the Nashville, Chattanooga and St. Louis railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazel%2C_Kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hazel's early economic foundation relied heavily on agriculture, particularly the farming of tobacco.",
